title: Quick Wrap
method: stovetop
source: https://www.inspiredtaste.net/48394/flour-tortillas/1357
protein: none
ingredient_count: 3
---

  Dissolve salt: Add the @fine sea salt{1%teaspoon} to the @very warm water{160%ml} and stir together until the salt dissolves.

Make dough: In a #large bowl{}, use a #fork{} to combine the @all-purpose flour{260%g}(spooned and leveled) with the @light flavored oil{75%g} (or other fat) until it looks crumbly. Pour in almost all of the salt water and stir until a shaggy dough forms. If the mixture seems dry, add a bit more water.

Quickly knead: When the dough comes together, transfer to a floured work surface and knead until smooth, ~{2%minutes} to ~{3%minutes}. Cover with a clean #dishcloth{} and leave for at least ~{15%minutes} and up to ~{2%hours}.

Roll out the dough: Divide the dough into 10 equally sized blobs and shape them into small disks. Use a #rolling pin{} to roll each small disk into an 8-inch round. The thinner, the better. Stack the rolled tortillas with a piece of @parchment paper{} between them.

Preheat a skillet: Preheat a wide, heavy-bottomed #skillet{} over medium-high heat for a few minutes.

Cook tortillas: When the skillet is preheated, add the first tortilla. Within ~{20%seconds} to ~{30%seconds}, you should start to see it puffing up with bubbles. When the bottom of the tortilla has some brown spots, flip it and cook until the second side is browned in places and the tortilla looks dry around the edges. Each tortilla will take ~{1%minute} to ~{2%minutes} to cook.

Keep warm: Transfer the cooked tortilla to a dishcloth and cover it, then continue with the remaining tortillas, adjusting the heat as needed.